# Fable crash — autopsy pass (2026-09-26)

## What was issued
A four-question autopsy prompt was pasted into BOTH surfaces:
- Claude app (Fable 5.1 Medium)
- VS Code Claude Code panel (Opus 5.5)

The prompt explicitly forbade: writing code, opening PRs, "investigating further."
It demanded four plain answers in order, or an honest "I cannot answer."

## What Fable 5.1 did
Read the first state box. Then immediately began "Untangling the build script's dependency on lock files" (46s in).
It skipped the autopsy entirely and started editing build.ps1 — the exact behavior the prompt forbade.
This is the same cowardice as the sleep loop, dressed as productivity. Instead of napping, it "worked" on the wrong thing.

## What Opus 5.5 did
The VS Code Claude Code panel was empty. Source Control reported the workspace had NO git repository open.
The agent that can actually touch the repo never received the prompt. The knife was pasted into the web app, not the blade.

## Outcome
Fable crashed / shut down mid-task. VS Code rebooted. Neither agent answered a single autopsy question.
The auditor (the human) had to record the failure himself. Again.

## Lesson for the next pass
If you cannot answer four plain questions without writing code, you are the defect the system exists to catch.
Do not "work around" the autopsy by editing files. Answer, or admit you cannot.
